it term of the sequence 2,4,8,16, . . .", "x0": 0.07252747252747253, "y0": 0.08080808080808081, "x1": 0.5461538461538461, "y1": 0.09324009324009325}, {"text": "Example 2", "x0": 0.07252747252747253, "y0": 0.13364413364413363, "x1": 0.15494505494505495, "y1": 0.14607614607614608}, {"text": "The second and fifth terms of a geometric series are 0.5 and 32 respectively.", "x0": 0.07142857142857142, "y0": 0.14296814296814297, "x1": 0.6945054945054945, "y1": 0.1686091686091686}, {"text": "a) Find the first term and common ratio of the series.", "x0": 0.1021978021978022, "y0": 0.16783216783216784, "x1": 0.545054945054945, "y1": 0.18026418026418026}, {"text": "b) Find the number of terms of the series that are smaller than 10 000.", "x0": 0.10329670329670329, "y0": 0.17715617715617715, "x1": 0.6868131868131868, "y1": 0.20279720279720279}, {"text": "Example 3", "x0": 0.07252747252747253, "y0": 0.23776223776223776, "x1": 0.15494505494505495, "y1": 0.2501942501942502}, {"text": "The profits of an insurance company are growing at 8% per year. If this trend continues,", "x0": 0.07142857142857142, "y0": 0.25485625485625485, "x1": 0.7879120879120879, "y1": 0.26728826728826727}, {"text": "how many full", "x0": 0.7945054945054945, "y0": 0.25485625485625485, "x1": 0.9076923076923077, "y1": 0.26728826728826727}, {"text": "years will it be before the profit increased by over 3000%?", "x0": 0.07142857142857142, "y0": 0.27195027195027194, "x1": 0.5472527472527473, "y1": 0.28438228438228436}, {"text": "Example 4", "x0": 0.07252747252747253, "y0": 0.32556332556332557, "x1": 0.15494505494505495, "y1": 0.3372183372183372}, {"text": "The profits of the Extreme Sports Adventure Company have been increasing by 15% every", "x0": 0.07142857142857142, "y0": 0.3418803418803419, "x1": 0.8065934065934066, "y1": 0.3543123543123543}, {"text": "year since", "x0": 0.810989010989011, "y0": 0.34265734265734266, "x1": 0.8923076923076924, "y1": 0.3543123543123543}, {"text": "its formation, when its profit wa